{
  "title": "What is Dask?",
  "text": "Community\nBlog\nDocs\nPowered by\n\nDask is an open-source project, which means there are a lot of people we’d like to thank from code contributors to corporate support to the projects using Dask. And, as a successful open-source project, there are some stats to crow about, too. Collectively, maintained by hundreds of open source contributors across dozens of companies.\n\nDask is supported by:\nAdd us to Dask support\nAnaconda\nDask is installed by default in Anaconda\nCoiled\nCoiled makes Dask infrastructure accessible to everyone\nNVIDIA\nDask integrates with RAPIDS cuDF, XGBoost, and RAPIDS cuML for GPU-accelerated data analytics and machine learning.\nSaturn Cloud\nSaturn Cloud lets users create Dask clusters in a hosted platform or within their own AWS accounts.\nCompanies\nPowered by Dask\nThese companies are part of the larger Dask community. They’re either well-integrated with Dask or use Dask to power components of their infrastructure.\nProjects Powered by Dask\nThese software projects are part of the larger Dask community. They’re either well-integrated with Dask or use Dask to power components of their infrastructure.\nDask Adoption Metrics\n6,049,226*\nMonthly downloads\n*Mostly bots\nBig Data Tools*\n*Python 2021 Developers Survey\nSee Python Developers Survey\nGet Started\nLatest\nCommunity\nGet Help\nPowered By\nDemo Day\nBlog\nDask Blog\nContribute\nBrand\nBrand Guidelines\ngo to github page\ngo to twitter page\ngo to youtube page\ngo to stackoverflow. page\ngo to dask discourse group page\n\nCopyright © 2026 Dask core developers. New-BSD Licensed.\n",
